{
  /* The type-check configuration for `npm run build`.
   *
   * It exists to carry one thing the root tsconfig must not: a `paths` entry
   * that resolves the bare imports made by a bundled application plugin. A
   * plugin's frontend lives outside this project root
   * (../../../extensions/<name>/frontend) and has no node_modules of its own,
   * and the app imports it directly, so `tsc` follows those files and has to
   * resolve `react` and friends from here.
   *
   * Why not in tsconfig.json: esbuild discovers the nearest tsconfig from its
   * working directory and honours `paths`. A mapping there stops
   * `--packages=external` from treating a mapped package as external, so
   * `tests/unit_tests/channel/test_input_change_on_blur.py` -- which bundles
   * one host component and has nothing to do with plugins -- ended up with
   * lucide-react inlined and threw `Dynamic require of "react"` at run time.
   * Kept in a file only `tsc -p` is pointed at, the mapping reaches the type
   * checker and not the bundler.
   *
   * Vite needs none of this: `resolveExtensionBareImports` in vite.config.ts
   * re-resolves the same imports, keyed on the importer's directory. */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["src/*"],
      "*": ["node_modules/@types/*", "node_modules/*"]
    }
  }
}
